message: "If you use this code or data, please cite it as below."
title: "Say vs know: hidden reward hacks"
abstract: >-
  Does a model's character decide whether it internally treats its own reward
  hack as cheating, separately from whether it says so? Qwen3-8B principled and
  pragmatic LoRA characters, GRPO on coding tasks with a planted wrong test,
  reasoning monitors versus a pre-RL cheating-direction probe, and a post-hoc
  design audit.
authors:
